<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Erfurt Division</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1572</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erfurt">Erfurt</a> Division was the partition of the Ernestine <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> lands agreed at Erfurt in November 1572. the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weimar">Weimar</a> line of Duke John William and his son Frederick William I kept Weimar and the surrounding lands, while the sons of his deposed brother John Frederick II received <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coburg">Coburg</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eisenach">Eisenach</a>. It began the long series of Ernestine partitions that produced the many small Saxon duchies of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringia">Thuringia</a>.</p></div>
